WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.070
- But I have to ask you this

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.310
'cause Joe Biden is now President

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.020
and I heard him say,
- What?

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.860
- I know it's exciting,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.693
but I heard--
- I thought

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:07.526
it was still out,

00:00:07.526 --> 00:00:09.116
I thought there was no conceding.

00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:10.719
- No, no, no.
- I didn't think,

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:11.552
so he won.
- He is President,

00:00:11.552 --> 00:00:12.970
I was there in the office with him.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:13.803
- Okay, great.

00:00:13.803 --> 00:00:14.636
- Yes.
- Oh, that's right!

00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:16.100
- And I was, and he did say

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.300
that Will and Grace did
more than anything else

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.640
to shift like how people
viewed gay marriage.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.473
- Yeah.

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:22.320
- And I never really thought about that,

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.930
but I think that's absolutely true.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:24.970
- Isn't that amazing?
- Especially reaching

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.050
on a broad scale, like so many.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.650
you're in the homes of, you know,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.483
- Yeah.
- all across America.

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:30.440
- I, I mean, look,

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.610
I got the, when I got the pilot,

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.780
which is the first episode,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.880
- Yeah.
- I was 27 years old.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:36.713
- Yeah.
- So just

00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:38.526
a couple of years ago, but I,

00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:39.359
(laughing)

00:00:39.359 --> 00:00:40.192
thanks, that took just a second.

00:00:40.192 --> 00:00:41.025
- Me too,

00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:42.550
me too.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.520
- But, no

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.700
and I was just happy to
get a job on a TV show.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.460
I had no idea that the by-product

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.440
would be something that
was bigger than all of us

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.160
and then I'm sitting at
home on the couch one day,

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.259
I remember this is when Joe
Biden was the Vice President

00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:55.617
and he said something on

00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.429
MSNBC or I don't know, some show

00:00:57.429 --> 00:01:00.710
and he was like, Will and Grace
did more to educate America

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:03.040
about the gay movement than anything

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.450
and I was like, what?

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.723
Like I was just crazy.
- I think it's true though,

00:01:06.723 --> 00:01:09.080
art does inspire like real life.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.630
Like I think, real life inspires art

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.490
I guess chicken and egg.
- Yeah.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.290
- But, but yeah, I, I
think it's absolutely true,

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.212
I just never thought about it

00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:16.045
until you said it.
- Also,

00:01:16.045 --> 00:01:16.878
it's the power of comedy.

00:01:16.878 --> 00:01:19.550
It's the power of, of comedy is, is

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.770
the ability to educate people
without them knowing it

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.610
because if they're enjoying you,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.440
there's no, you can't,

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.000
- Yeah.
- you can't combat that,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.550
right, right?
- Yeah, I agree.

